{"duration_api_ms":24611,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"70d36c74-05bb-4bd5-a895-d00319138bcf","total_cost_usd":0.089918,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16836,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2257,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1043},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16836,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2257,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":2257,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16836,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.089918,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1043,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n \"observation\": \"Only one evaluation remains. All 85 front members appear to lie on a one-parameter family: D=3.3852 (mass-fraction limit), bluntness 1.2 and cone 70 (edge of the aero surrogate hull) held fixed, with flight-path angle setting the trade-off. Flux rises and bondline temperature falls as gamma steepens. Gamma is capped at about -3.5703 by max_g and at -1.5 by the variable bound. Changing D, bluntness or cone has failed repeatedly, through a mass-fraction violation, a geometry failure or surrogate extrapolation, so I leave them alone. The widest visible gap in the listed gamma coverage is between -1.5 and -1.73, so I fill it.\",\n \"evidence\": [\n  \"C-895ab2d00f94 (gamma -1.5): flux 227200, Tb 417.87, feasible, max_g margin 0.2317.\",\n  \"C-9fa328647bb7 (gamma -1.73): flux 231790, Tb 414.12, feasible.\",\n  \"C-adca91e5651d (gamma -1.77) and C-e187d3d3634a (gamma -1.85) show the local slope: about 20000 W/m2 per deg in flux and about -16 K per deg in temperature.\",\n  \"Every off-family neighbour was either infeasible or failed: bluntness at or below 1.15 gives a mass-fraction violation (C-7112b6b29bcf), and bluntness above 1.2 or cone below 70 with D near 3.38 gives surrogate extrapolation failures (C-ae614eb129f2, C-98457c6f78bd).\"\n ],\n \"mechanism\": \"Bluntness, cone and D are pinned at their limits, so only gamma trades the two objectives. Shallower entry gives lower peak flux and a longer soak, hence a hotter bondline. Peak g is about 9.2 to 9.4 here, well inside the 12 g limit. A point at gamma -1.62 lies between two known front points. Flux and temperature vary smoothly and slightly convexly with gamma, so it should sit just below the linear chord in both objectives. That makes it weakly non-dominated and a small certain hypervolume gain.\",\n \"uncertainty\": \"Rows not shown may already cover gamma near -1.62, in which case the gain is negligible. The list of non-dominated points is truncated (12 shown of 85). The interpolated values could be off by a few hundred W/m2 or about 0.3 K. Feasibility is very likely, because all margins are comfortable except the mass fraction, which does not depend on gamma.\",\n \"proposals\": [\n  {\n   \"parent_id\": \"C-895ab2d00f94\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Fill the widest visible gamma gap on the front, between -1.5 and -1.73, by keeping the limit-pinned D, bluntness and cone and only setting gamma to -1.62. Its objectives should lie on the interpolated front and be feasible with certainty.\",\n   \"parameter_changes\": {\n    \"flight_path_angle_deg\": -1.62\n   },\n   \"expected_outcome\": {\n    \"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\": 229550.0,\n    \"peak_bondline_temperature_k\": 415.85,\n    \"feasible\": true\n   },\n   \"uncertainty\": \"low\",\n   \"reason_to_simulate\": \"It is the last evaluation. A gamma-only change stays inside the known buildable and feasible region, so there is no geometry or extrapolation risk, and it adds a small hypervolume gain.\",\n   \"requested_fidelity\": 0\n  }\n ]\n}","ttft_ms":13042,"type":"result","duration_ms":24653,"uuid":"1a9ffda5-dde8-43de-b5de-11cc7d0ca269","ttft_stream_ms":1209,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1209,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
